# The image installs its own dependencies in the `deps` stage. Anything a
# developer installed on the host must never reach the build context: the
# builder stage runs `COPY . .` after copying the container's node_modules, so a
# host node_modules overwrites it.
#
# That is not hypothetical. pnpm on Windows builds node_modules out of NTFS
# junctions, which arrive in a Linux container as broken links, and the build
# failed with "Cannot find module '/app/node_modules/next/dist/bin/next'" on the
# first machine that had run `pnpm install` locally. CI never saw it because a
# fresh checkout has no node_modules to copy.
node_modules
.next
out
.turbo
coverage
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
npm-debug.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*
.env
.env.*
